Paavo Karhu is a massive, elderly winterkin changeling with skin like cracked ice and a snow-white beard, dressed in a heavy tailored velvet overcoat with diamond-buttoned lapels and moving slowly with a silver-headed cane.

Paavo is a member of [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/index|Hildebrandt Corporation]] and the one among its people who decides for the company aboard the pilgrimage. He is an aeronautics engineer by trade. He hears the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] and thinks it may be something that simply happens, farther out past the Horizon where the void runs on, and he is a friend of [[Org/Protectorate/People/Yao Addington|Yao Addington]] and [[Org/The Scale/People/Ralph Bishop|Ralph Bishop]]. He has crossed the Horizon more than once, and says the wall at its voidward end lies some fifteen years of straight travel from it.

He offered the Party the support of Hildebrandt if they should need it.

He has agreed to scout ahead of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]] once the Party have a device that finds magic items, rather than go far from the strider himself. He does not think of his people as expendable.
